     "en": "Sweets for Nani Maa"
    },
    "text": {
     "en": "Chirag and Nandini brought sweets and books for Nani Maa. How many in all? How many are left after eating some?"
    }
   },
   {
    "id": "explain",
    "type": "explanation",
    "provenance": "original",
    "keepEnglishTerms": [
     "total",
     "left",
     "altogether"
    ],
    "text": {
     "en": "A word problem tells a story with numbers. Read it twice slowly.\nIf the story says altogether or total, we add. If it says left or how many more, we subtract.\nNandini had 7 balushahi and Chirag had 5. Altogether they have 7 + 5 = 12.\nChirag ate 5 from 12, so 12 - 5 = 7 are left.\nDraw dots or tick marks to help you picture the story.\nAlways write the answer with the thing counted, like 12 balushahi."
    }
